Seed an item with stock=5, run the app under a threaded server, and write a pytest that fires 50 concurrent purchases and demonstrates overselling (stock goes negative or >5 successes) BEFORE the fix; keep that as a regression test that now asserts the correct behavior after you fix it with an atomic conditional UPDATE (UPDATE items SET stock=stock-1 WHERE id=? AND stock>0 checking rowcount). Final state: exactly 5 successes, 45 sold_out, stock 0, pytest green.

